{arial}Decoding Centre: Papyrus 5
Message: PAPY-707
Operator: Corporal Sipher

from: {arialbld}Kurt Rorscham{arial}
Diffa Town Hall








The radio just won't shut up about you... the whole day long! I certainly don't recommend letting it all get to your head, {rank}, until now you've just had what we call "beginner's luck", but things are getting bad and you're gonna want to cut down on your sunbathing, because the Psychos listen to the radio too and they don't exactly love you. Even the big boss got word of it: Magnus Von Tekton himself. He has requested that they bring him your scalp on his birthday, in 14 days...

300km separate us from a pocket of Jaffari resistance, 300km of territory infested with Psycho tanks as hard as a rhino's butt, against which our own armor is as effective as a wet newspaper. 

Unfortunately our reinforcements aren't arriving anymore, as the sea is teeming with submarines straight out of {arialbld}Birakem{arial}, a naval base very dear to Tankred Von Tekton. 

The High Command has made the capture of this island Top Priority. What the High Command fails to mention is that Birakem's airspace is completely covered by Karlo's air forces based at {arialbld}Moktar{arial}.

In short your mission is to surf right into the middle of the jaws of blood-thirsty sharks having your neck eaten alive by maniacal wasps.

{arialbld}Take note:{arial}

Within the hour you will get to the port of {arialbld}Constantine{arial}, my headquarters being at {arialbld}Diffa{arial}, a bit more to the north-west. Constantine has a small airfield which will allow you to make aerial reconnaissances of the area. Also Alex Kolman has really spoiled you with three naval destroyers equipped with a brand new "aquatic radar" system called {arialbld}SONAR{arial} (directions for use below). 














{center}{device22}












Lucky bastard, I don't have anything close to that! We're launching an amphibian operation to land on Moktar ASAP, and I'd appreciate it if you could blow up those sharks around my ships. It's a team sport {name} and there are no replacements, so if one of us breaks a leg, both our scalps will decorate a Psycho chimney in Tektonia.


{offset50}Commander of the 1st Schyzo Army at Jaffar

{arialbld}Kurt Rorscham{arial} 



{offset150}{signature5}
{offset0}


